---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import siteConfig from '../data/site-config.json';

const lastUpdated = 'January 28, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for Best US National Parks. Please read these terms carefully before using our website."
>
  <div class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-display font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
          Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-500 mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p>
            Welcome to {siteConfig.name}. By accessing or using our website at {siteConfig.url},
            you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms,
            please do not use our website.
          </p>

          <h2>Use of Website</h2>
          <p>
            You may use our website for lawful purposes only. You agree not to:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Use the website in any way that violates applicable laws or regulations</li>
            <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the website</li>
            <li>Use automated systems to scrape or collect content without permission</li>
            <li>Transmit any malicious code, viruses, or harmful content</li>
            <li>Impersonate any person or entity</li>
            <li>Interfere with the proper functioning of the website</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Content and Information</h2>
          <p>
            The information on this website is provided for general informational purposes only.
            While we strive to keep information accurate and up-to-date, we make no warranties
            about the completeness, reliability, or accuracy of this information.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Important:</strong> National park conditions, regulations, fees, and hours
            change frequently. Always verify current information with the official National Park
            Service website (nps.gov) before planning your visit.
          </p>

          <h2>Not Affiliated with NPS</h2>
          <p>
            {siteConfig.name} is an independent website and is <strong>not affiliated with,
            endorsed by, or connected to the National Park Service</strong>, the U.S. Department
            of the Interior, or any government agency. Any views or opinions expressed on this
            website are our own.
          </p>

          <h2>User Submissions</h2>
          <p>
            When you submit tips, corrections, photos, or other content to our website, you:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Grant us a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, modify, and publish your submission</li>
            <li>Confirm that you own the content or have permission to submit it</li>
            <li>Understand that we may edit submissions for clarity, accuracy, or length</li>
            <li>Agree that we are not obligated to use or publish any submission</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p>
            The content on this website, including text, graphics, logos, and images, is owned by
            {siteConfig.name} or used with permission. You may not reproduce, distribute, or create
            derivative works from our content without written permission.
          </p>
          <p>
            Park photographs may be subject to National Park Service usage guidelines or third-party
            copyrights. AI-generated images on this site are clearly identified as such.
          </p>

          <h2>Affiliate Links and Advertising</h2>
          <p>
            Our website may contain affiliate links to products, services, and booking platforms.
            If you make a purchase through these links, we may earn a commission at no additional
            cost to you.
          </p>
          <p>
            We only recommend products and services we believe provide value to our visitors.
            However, affiliate relationships do not influence our editorial content or reviews.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
          <p>
            Our website contains links to third-party websites, including the National Park Service,
            Recreation.gov, and various travel services. We are not responsible for the content,
            privacy practices, or terms of service of these external sites.
          </p>

          <h2>Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
          <p>
            This website is provided "as is" without any warranties, express or implied. We do not
            warrant that:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>The website will be available at all times or free from errors</li>
            <li>Information on the website is complete, accurate, or current</li>
            <li>The website is free from viruses or harmful components</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, {siteConfig.name} shall not be liable for any
            indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from your use of this
            website, including but not limited to:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Errors or inaccuracies in content</li>
            <li>Personal injury or property damage resulting from your park visits</li>
            <li>Unauthorized access to your personal information</li>
            <li>Any interruption or cessation of our services</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>Safety Notice:</strong> National parks contain inherent risks including wildlife,
            extreme weather, difficult terrain, and remote locations. Always prepare adequately,
            follow park regulations, and make safety your top priority.
          </p>

          <h2>Indemnification</h2>
          <p>
            You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {siteConfig.name} and its owners from any
            claims, damages, or expenses arising from your use of the website or violation of
            these terms.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to Terms</h2>
          <p>
            We reserve the right to modify these Terms of Service at any time. Changes will be
            effective immediately upon posting to this page. Your continued use of the website
            after changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.
          </p>

          <h2>Governing Law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws
            of the United States, without regard to conflict of law principles.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have any questions about these Terms of Service, please contact us at:
          </p>
          <p>
            Email: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`} class="link-primary">{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    @apply text-2xl font-display font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4;
  }
  .prose p {
    @apply text-gray-700 mb-4;
  }
  .prose ul {
    @apply list-disc list-inside mb-6 space-y-1;
  }
  .prose li {
    @apply text-gray-700;
  }
</style>
